  "synonym_discrimination": null,
  "usage_note": "Everyday speech generally uses **who** for both subject and object; **whom** is kept mainly in formal writing and directly after a preposition (*to whom it may concern*). With the preposition at the end of the clause instead, **who** is standard even in careful writing: *who did you speak to?*",
